                    <p class="text-slate-700">Investor B bought stock at $100 that dropped to $50 but can't sell it. "If I sell now, I'll lose $5,000." But economically, the $5,000 loss is already sunk cost that cannot be recovered. A rational micro actor should only consider: "If I move the remaining $5,000 to another stock, can I earn higher returns?"</p>
